6489244 #edb/ref 1071 "Express $\\frac{1}{64}$ as a base raised to a negative exponent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489244 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "955d0666-e318-54f6-bac2-1bee61b1768a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489244 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write $\\frac{1}{64}$ as a power with a negative exponent.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{64} & =\\frac{1\\times 1\\times 1}{4\\times 4\\times 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the reciprocal of the base $(\\frac{1}{4}),$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the *opposite* sign $(-3),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{3}={4}^{-3}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489296 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489296 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71764" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489296 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489296 #edb/ref 1071 "${(\\frac{3}{4})}^{-2}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489296 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fe935012-f0c6-58bc-9344-9d20da9c881b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489296 #edb/ref 1074 "We find the reciprocal of the base $(\\frac{3}{4})$, and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the *opposite* sign $(+2)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{-2} & ={(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489356 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489367 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489356 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b1e8a66e-55d5-5db0-9038-791aff3a99ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489356 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489365 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d4caf3a0-5c40-55ce-be61-96aecb662c7e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489365 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489367 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489365 #edb/r